From: fanha99 <fanha99@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: 1024-entry RXDMA buffer ring on QCN6122 in the 256M profile

999-990 gives both radios of a 256 MiB board a 512-entry RXDMA buffer
ring. On a Xiaomi CR8806 (IPQ5018 + QCN6122, NSS Wi-Fi offload) the
5 GHz QCN6122 ring runs out under upload bursts: five rounds of iperf3
upload at 300-450 Mbit/s gave 78k RXDMA overflows. With 1024 entries
the same load gave 433, with 2048 49-102. The 2.4 GHz IPQ5018 radio
saw no overflow at 512.

Size the ring per radio: 1024 for QCN6122, DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE for
the rest. The NSS Wi-Fi datapath sizes its RX descriptor pool from the
same value, so use it there too. 2048 on both radios held about 3000
more 4 KiB buffers and cost ~10 MiB of MemAvailable; 1024 on QCN6122
alone adds 512 buffers.

Signed-off-by: fanha99 <fanha99@hotmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
@@ -250,6 +250,19 @@
 #endif
 #define DP_RXDMA_REFILL_RING_SIZE	ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_REFILL_RING_SIZE
 #define DP_RXDMA_NSS_REFILL_RING_SIZE	ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_NSS_REFILL_RING_SIZE
+/* With the 256M profile, give the 5 GHz QCN6122 radio a 1024-entry RXDMA
+ * buffer ring: at 512 it runs out under upload bursts (RXDMA overflow).
+ * The IPQ5018 2.4 GHz radio does not get near 512 and keeps it. The NSS
+ * Wi-Fi datapath sizes its RX descriptor pool from the same value.
+ */
+#ifdef CPTCFG_ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_256M
+#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE_QCN6122	1024
+#define ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE(ab) \
+	((ab)->hw_rev == ATH11K_HW_QCN6122_HW10 ? \
+	 DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE_QCN6122 : DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE)
+#else
+#define ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE(ab)	DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE
+#endif
 #ifdef CPTCFG_ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_256M
 #define DP_RXDMA_ERR_DST_RING_SIZE	128
 #else
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -673,7 +673,7 @@
 	ret = ath11k_dp_srng_setup(ar->ab,
 				   &dp->rx_refill_buf_ring.refill_buf_ring,
 				   HAL_RXDMA_BUF, 0,
-				   dp->mac_id, DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE);
+				   dp->mac_id, ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE(ab));
 	if (ret) {
 		ath11k_warn(ar->ab, "failed to setup rx_refill_buf_ring\n");
 		return ret;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -3279,7 +3279,7 @@
 	pdevmsg->radio_id = radio_id;
 	pdevmsg->lmac_id = ar->lmac_id;
 	pdevmsg->target_pdev_id = ar->pdev->pdev_id;
-	pdevmsg->num_rx_swdesc = WIFILI_RX_DESC_POOL_WEIGHT * DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE;
+	pdevmsg->num_rx_swdesc = WIFILI_RX_DESC_POOL_WEIGHT * ATH11K_DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE(ab);
 	pdevmsg->scheme_id = scheme_id;
 
 	/* Store rxdma ring info to the message */
